{
  "_what": "Layers 1 and 2 as CATALOGUES rather than as lookups. derive-provenance asks 'does this recipe have a source'; to ask the opposite — 'does this source have a recipe' — the layers have to exist as complete lists, and layers 1 and 2 only existed here as a hand table and as anchors keyed by our own recipe ids.",
  "_why": "Without this the component set can be JUSTIFIED but not EXACT. Every recipe naming a source proves nothing was invented; only the reverse direction proves nothing was missed, and 'nothing was missed' is the claim that makes a set derived rather than chosen.",
  "_honesty": "Captured snapshots with URLs, like openui-names.json and service-systems.json. The HTML list is deliberately the elements that RENDER A CONTROL OR A VISIBLE STRUCTURE — not all ~110 elements, because <head>, <script> and <template> are not components and padding the denominator with them would flatter the coverage number.",
